      "dom_id": "step-q20599",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+8z=90 \\\\  & y+4z=50 \\\\  & z=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 & 90 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 50 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 & 90 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 50 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 & 90 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-8){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=-10 \\\\  & y=10 \\\\  & z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-10$, $y=10$, and $z=10.$ Or, in vector form $⟨-10,10,10⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
