    "q-20267": {
      "dom_id": "step-q20267",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=2 \\\\  & x+2y+z=0 \\\\  & x+y+2z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=3 \\\\  & y=-2 \\\\  & z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=3$, $y=-2$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨3,-2,1⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-20267-a",
