    "q-74618": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74618",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+5z=1 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=-1 \\\\ 6y+12z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74618-a",
              "type": "math",
