    "q-74610": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74610",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x+6y+z=18 \\\\ 6x-36y-6z=-108 \\\\ -4x+24y+4z=72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 1 & 18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 1 & 18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-74610-a",
